      "rationale": "Residues 290 and 291 are both within ECL4 (282\u2013310), confirmed extracellular by the authoritative landmarks. Python confirms residue 290 = E and residue 291 = H. The junction is \u22659 aa from either TM boundary, well within the 29-residue loop, and the HA-tagged construct traffics to the surface and supports functional readouts. This exact junction is independently corroborated by L2, L3, L4, L5, and L6 with HA and FLAG tags across multiple labs. Full-length SERINC5 with HA tag inserted between residues 290 and 291 (SERINC5(iHA)) expressed in human cells; used to study surface expression and Nef-mediated downregulation. The junction is explicitly named in the paper. ECL4 (282\u2013310) is confirmed extracellular by the authoritative topology landmarks; residue 290 (E) sits 9 aa from TM7 end (281) and 20 aa from TM8 start (311).",
