      "rationale": "The authoritative topology places residues 413\u2013423 in ECL5 (extracellular), so a C-terminal tag appended after residue 423 (P) is on the extracellular face. Python confirms residue 423 = P. The tag is 11 aa from TM9 end (412), satisfying the \u22653 aa distance constraint. L4 explicitly describes this construct as carrying a C-terminal HA in addition to the internal FLAG, and it was used in functional HIV infectivity assays. Full-length SERINC5 bearing both an internal FLAG (290/291) and a C-terminal HA tag (SERINC5-iFLAG, HA) was expressed in HEK293T cells and used in HIV-1 infectivity assays. The C-terminus (residue 423, P) falls within ECL5 (413\u2013423), which is extracellular per the authoritative topology landmarks; TM9 ends at 412, placing the tag 11 aa from the last TM boundary.",
